<title>SOUTH KOREA: LG, IBM Korea to form PC joint venture.</title>
<headline>LG, IBM Korea to form PC joint venture.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1996-10-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>LG Electronics, a unit of South Korea's LG Group, said in a statement on Tuesday that it will set up a joint venture with IBM Korea to make personal computers (PC) and parts.</p>
<p>LG-IBM PC Co will be capitalised at $30 million or 24.3 billion won with IBM Korea taking a 51 percent stake and LG the rest, the statement said.  </p>
<p>A LG Electronics spokesman said the joint venture would initially utilise existing LG production lines to make notebook PCs, desk-top PCs, PC servers and computer accessories.</p>
<p>Output will be marketed under the LG-IBM brand name for the domestic market and for export. LG will continue to produce its own brand name products for export.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5647</p>
